   "text": {
    "L1": "A trader kept a parrot in a golden cage. The parrot wanted freedom.",
    "L2": "It sent a message to a forest parrot. The forest parrot showed a clever plan.",
    "L3": "The forest parrot fell and lay still, but it was only pretending.",
    "L4": "The caged parrot copied the trick. The trader thought it was dead and opened the cage.",
    "L5": "The parrot flew away. It used its brain, not its strength, to become free.",
    "L6": "So the forest parrot did not really die. That is why the story is clever, not sad.",
    "L7": "Remember: say the words, but tell a person. We say, 'He said, “Fly away.”'",
    "L8": "We say, 'He told the parrot the plan.' Now show what you understood."
   },
